Record the system prompt from every shape the SDK accepts, and stop recording a
label as one. A custom prompt holds the real, full text under `prompt` and was
dropped entirely, while the identical content passed as a bare string was
captured — so which of the two API shapes a caller reached for decided whether it
appeared. The preset form was recorded as the synthetic instruction text `preset:
claude_code`, which is a name rather than anything the model was told; it and the
file form's path are now recorded as what they are, a part naming the prompt's
source. The agent span receives `gen_ai.system_instructions` too, which it never
did.
